{
  "$comment": "The machine-readable field-class manifest for heartbeat.v2.json. EVERY leaf in the schema appears exactly once, here or in `reserved`; scripts/check-field-classes.ts fails the build on any drift in either direction. Value classes: count | ratio | bucket | enum | bool | version | duration. Temporal classes: delta | gauge — and NOTHING else. `cumulative` is deliberately NOT a legal value: normalisation happens at the emitter (gate G2), so no lifetime counter ever reaches the wire. There is deliberately NO `opaque-id` class (gate G1b chose three documented per-product identities over a shared install_group field); adding one re-opens that gate. Envelope descriptors carry temporal `gauge` because they are per-document snapshots that are never summed — docs/FIELDS.md writes their temporal as '—', which this vocabulary cannot express. THIS MANIFEST AND ITS CHECK ENFORCE SHAPE, NOT PRIVACY: see `limits` below.",
  "schema": "heartbeat.v2.json",
  "schema_version": 2,
  "limits": "A mechanical check cannot tell a privacy-safe count from a privacy-hostile one. `metrics.database_oid: integer` classed `count`+`delta` passes every rule in this file. Any NEW or RECLASSIFIED leaf therefore requires a named human privacy review recorded in the pull request. Do not describe this manifest, or its CI check, as enforcing privacy.",
  "reserved": {
    "instance_id": {
      "reason": "Identity, not a metric. It has no value class by design — the class vocabulary has no identifier member, and adding one re-opens gate G1b. Fenced instead by an exact grammar: the UUIDv4 pattern pinned in the schema, which no name, label or encoded hostname satisfies.",
      "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-4[0-9a-f]{3}-[89ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$"
    },
    "day": {
      "reason": "The document's aggregation key, not a metric. Fenced by an exact calendar-day grammar.",
      "pattern": "^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$"
    }
  },
  "envelope": {
